d a new chapter</a> to the Cargo book, <a href=3D"https://doc.rust-lang.org=
/stable/cargo/guide/build-performance.html">=E2=80=9COptimizing Build Perfo=
rmance=E2=80=9D</a>.</li></ul><p><a id=3D"1.92.0-Rustdoc"></a></p><h2 id=3D=
"rustdoc" data-eusoft-scrollable-element=3D"1">Rustdoc
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"https://releases.rs/docs/1.92.0/#rustdoc">#</a>=
</h2><ul><li><a href=3D"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/145898">If a=
 trait item appears in rustdoc search, hide the corresponding impl items</a=
>. Previously a search for =E2=80=9Clast=E2=80=9D would show both <code>Ite=
rator::last</code> as well as impl methods like <code>std::vec::IntoIter::l=
ast</code>. Now these impl methods will be hidden, freeing up space for inh=
erent methods like <code>BTreeSet::last</code>.</li><li><a href=3D"https://=
github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/147860">Relax rules for identifiers in searc=
h</a>. Previously you could only search for identifiers that were valid in =
rust code, now searches only need to be valid as part of an identifier. For=
 example, you can now perform a search that starts with a digit.</li></ul><=
p><a id=3D"1.92.0-Compatibility-Notes"></a></p><h2 id=3D"compatibility-note=
s" data-eusoft-scrollable-element=3D"1">Compatibility Notes
<a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"https://releases.rs/docs/1.92.0/#compatibility-=
notes">#</a></h2><ul><li><a href=3D"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/=
143613">Fix backtraces with <code>-C panic=3Dabort</code> on Linux by gener=
ating unwind tables by default</a>. Build with <code>-C force-unwind-tables=
=3Dno</code> to keep omitting unwind tables.</li></ul><ul><li>As part of th=
e larger effort refactoring compiler built-in attributes and their diagnost=
ics, <a href=3D"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/143857">the future-c=
ompatibility lint <code>invalid_macro_export_arguments</code> is upgraded t=
o deny-by-default and will be reported in dependencies too.</a></li><li><a =
href=3D"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/145071">Update the minimum e=
xternal LLVM to 20</a></li><li><a href=3D"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust=
/pull/145608">Prevent downstream <code>impl DerefMut for Pin&lt;LocalType&g=
t;</code></a></li><li><a href=3D"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/145=
838">Don=E2=80=99t apply temporary lifetime extension rules to the argument=
s of non-extended <code>pin!</code> and formatting macros</a></li></ul></ar=
